rkisp: guard the v39 LSC config against missing LUT buffers.

Reproduced on the SMT1019: if the ISP params stream restarts while the
rkaiq 3A engine is mid-reinitialization (kernel logs "waiting on params
stream off event timeout"), the next STREAMON runs
rkisp_params_first_cfg_v39 -> isp_lsc_config -> isp_lsc_matrix_cfg_ddr
with buf_lsclut[].vaddr == NULL and Oopses on the table write. Skip the
config cycle instead; a healthy params cycle reconfigures LSC.

--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/isp/isp_params_v39.c	2026-07-26 10:26:18
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/isp/isp_params_v39.c	2026-07-26 10:26:18
@@ -521,6 +521,14 @@
 	memset(&index[0], 0, sizeof(index));
 	buf_idx = (priv_val->buf_lsclut_idx++) % ISP39_LSC_LUT_BUF_NUM;
 	buf_vaddr = priv_val->buf_lsclut[buf_idx].vaddr;
+	/* The LUT buffers can be gone when params restart while the 3A engine
+	 * is mid-reinit (observed: NULL deref Oops here on STREAMON after
+	 * "waiting on params stream off event timeout"). Skip this cycle —
+	 * the next healthy params cycle reconfigures LSC. */
+	if (!buf_vaddr) {
+		WARN_ONCE(1, "rkisp: lsc lut buffer not allocated, skip lsc config\n");
+		return;
+	}
 
 	vaddr[0] = buf_vaddr;
 	vaddr[1] = buf_vaddr + ISP39_LSC_LUT_TBL_SIZE;
